       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's half-life is long, at 30 to 50 hours, so the effects could last a long time. Nothing in the patient's profile (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function) would justify a higher dose.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg PO daily**, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg PO daily**, the maximum dose.\n- A different drug or dose, if you meant something else.\n\nIf 50 mg is intentional, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
